  "sourceData": {
    "answer": "to{} discover/find-(e.g.-an-error-in-a-book)/come-across/detect/spot | locate/find-(e.g.-something-missing)/find-fault | to-be:used-to-seeing/familiar-with",
    "mnemonic": "You know that <ja>付ける</ja> means \"to attach\" and that <ja>見</ja> means \"see.\" So, when you attach your seeing to something, it's like you're looking around trying <vocabulary>to find</vocabulary> something. When you find what you're looking for, imagine your eyeballs flying out and attaching to that item, then yelling \"I FOUND IT!\"\n\nYou'll usually see this word with the <ja>付</ja> in kana, so <ja>見つける</ja>.",
    "readingMnemonic": "The readings come from <ja>見る</ja> and <ja>付ける</ja>. If you use those readings, you'll be able to read this word too."
